NNOOTTEESS
     The breakpoint instruction is sscc #00xx8811 and single stepping
     uses the hardware single-step trap; sscc and block-move in-
     structions cannot be stepped that way, so ddbb places a tem-
     porary breakpoint after them instead.

     The :kk command is accepted but sends no signal.  Registers
     live in the user area, so patching them takes effect when
     the child next runs.
